- Viewer overlay nav buttons (`BtnGalleryPrev` / `BtnGalleryNext` / `BtnGalleryClose` in `GrdViewerOverlayNav`): `ViewerOverlayButtonStyle` / `ViewerOverlayCloseButtonStyle` from `Resources/ViewerOverlayStyles.xaml` — translucent black circular plates (40 Prev/Next, 36 Close; hit ≥44), 16px Fluent glyph, fixed Light/Dark brushes, HighContrast uses `SystemColorButtonFace` / `ButtonText` / `Highlight` + 2px border. Auto-hide after 2.5s idle (`ViewerOverlayChrome` / `ViewerOverlayAutoHide`: 200ms out / 100ms in; never while hovered/focused, Narrator on, or animations off; keep tab order when faded). Prev/Next disabled on ends. When left-docked Details is open, `BtnGalleryPrev` / `BtnGalleryWindowPrev` left margin is `GalleryPrevMargin` / `ViewerDetailsLayout.PrevMargin` (host inset + panel width + gap) so the plate sits past the card's right edge — do not leave it at 16 over Histogram/Gamut. Tooltips include Left/Right/Esc. Style is **reusable** (Width/Height set plate size; override Background/BorderBrush/Foreground for accent-on Info, 24px remove, volume pill) — do not fork a second circular chrome pack.
- Overlay / GalleryWindow **Details / Info** is a single floating `ViewerDetailsCard` in `GrdViewerLeftChrome` **Grid row 1 under the toolbar** (`AttachInFlow` for MaxHeight; RowSpacing 8) — layout-driven dock so reopen via I / Ctrl+D / Info pill cannot jump. ~270 epx, `ViewerDetailsSurfaceBrush`. MaxHeight grows to the bottom margin (not a short fixed Height). Dense: filename once in title (+ copy); File = path+icons + meta; Color & HDR = inline label+value 2-col with HDR on its own full-width row (hide section when no rows; ignore gamut-only); Expander headers ~24px transparent; footer ~28px icon+short labels; Histogram compact plot ~90px (Compact hides duplicate format·index·size under the plot and the Gamut chart's `TxtGamutTitle` — expander headers already name those sections). File + Color & HDR + Histogram should fit without scrolling at ~1200×800. Toggle with toolbar **Info** pill (`I` / `Ctrl+D` / `Alt+Enter`; `ShowDetails`). Esc closes card first. Never cover toolbar or `MediaPlayer` transport. Video open must never maximize / full-window (`ViewerMediaElement.SuppressFullWindow`; GalleryWindow size ≤90% work area). Animated GIF stills keep autoplay via `GifFrames` delays + composite frames (`GifPlaying`); Pause keeps `GifFrameIndex` instead of restarting `BitmapImage`. `GalleryStillSurface` loads frames once with `TryRenderAll` and applies ticks from that cache — play `GifFrameIndex` ticks must not `RefreshAsync` / cancel that load while the cache is empty (`ShouldApplyGifTick` / `ShouldStartGifCompositeLoad`). The delay clock waits until composites exist (`ShouldRunGifPlayLoop` / `NotifyGifCompositeReady`) so Pause/slider during load keep frame 0. Library and Tags `CloseOverlay` plus `GalleryWindow` Closed call `StopGifPlayback`; `Bind(null)` also stops that clock so a late `NotifyGifCompositeReady` cannot keep the VM alive after Esc/close. Applying a cached GIF cancels a stale other-path `_gifLoadCts` (`ShouldCancelStaleGifLoad`). `TryRenderAll` honors the load cancel token. `FitsCacheBudget` is overflow-safe (divide, not `width*height*4*frames` which wraps) and caps 256 MB / 2048 frames. `FitsFramePixels` caps image-descriptor `fw*fh` the same way so `DecodeLzw` / `Blit` cannot allocate ~2 GB off a small logical screen — oversized GIFs skip scrub (`gifInfo` null) and stay on the non-scrub still path with `ToStillImage(..., animateGif: true)` so `BitmapImage` still autoplays. Failed `TryRenderAll` after scrub was offered abandons chrome (`AbandonGifScrub` / `ShouldAbandonScrubOnFailedComposite`) and falls back to `ToStillImage(..., animateGif: true)`. Scrub `ToStillImage` keeps `AutoPlay` off. Switching onto a GIF still bumps the HDR `_epoch` (`ShouldBumpHdrEpochOnGifStillRefresh`) so a late WIC/scRGB present cannot replace `ImgStill`, without cancelling `TryRenderAll`. Overlay (`BrdGifScrub` / `BtnGifPlay` / `BtnGifPause` / `BtnGifPrevFrame` / `SldGifFrame` / `BtnGifNextFrame` / `TxtGifFrame`) and `GalleryWindow` (`BrdGalleryWindowGifScrub` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPlay` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPause` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifPrevFrame` / `SldGalleryWindowGifFrame` / `BtnGalleryWindowGifNextFrame` / `TxtGalleryWindowGifFrame`) add Pause / Play / prev-next frame / timeline on **local hydrated** `.gif` only (`GifFrames.CanScrub`, two or more frames) — do not recall On-Demand to scrub, and do not put GIF chrome over `MediaPlayer` transport. Overlay / GalleryWindow PreviewKeyDown must not mark Left/Right handled while `SldGifFrame` / `SldGalleryWindowGifFrame` is focused (`PassesGifSliderArrows`) — the slider nudges the frame; Left/Right elsewhere still change the asset. `GalleryWindow` Details uses the same floating `ViewerDetailsCard` (`ScrViewerDetails`) — not a layout-consuming right column. Long prompt/description scrolls inside the card. The top-left Info chrome bar stays compact and opaque (`SolidBackgroundFillColorSecondaryBrush`) — not over `MediaPlayer` transport (settings / seek). Tall generation text scrolls inside the card Expanders; do not grow a layout row forever. Overlay / `GalleryWindow` stills use **1:1 / Fit / Fill** (`GalleryScale`, Ctrl+1/2/3, Fluent Regular Size16 + text: `RatioOneToOne` / `ScaleFit` / `ScaleFill`). **1:1** is one device pixel per oriented image pixel (`ActualDipSize` = pixels / raster scale). Size the Image to those DIPs and use `Stretch.Uniform` — `Stretch.None` paints PixelWidth DIPs and clips at >100% DPI. Not catalog Width/Height (unoriented). **Fill** covers the viewport (crop overflow), **centers** the cover crop (`CoverCenterOffset` / `InitialScrollOffset`), and pans the overflow. Recenter/reset pinch and scroll when the still, scale, or viewport size changes so a prior pan does not stick. 1:1 and Fill pan with **left-click drag** (`GalleryScale.UsesPointerCapturePan`) and **touch/pen** ManipulationDelta (`DragPan`); pinch scale is `GalleryScale.PinchZoom` (1–8) on `GalleryStillSurface` (Fit letterboxes until pinch). A pinch frame uses one `ChangeView` via `PinchThenDrag` — do not DragPan from stale `HorizontalOffset` after pinch. Pen stays off pointer-capture pan so it does not pan twice. Details and an HDR line come from `GalleryPresent` + `HdrFile` / `AvifFile` (header-only; skip online-only). Magick TGA/EXR stay out. Radiance `.hdr` is isolated C# RGBE (`RadianceFile`). Radiance and OpenEXR (`ExrFile` → bundled OpenEXRCore `palace_exr.dll` via `ExrNative`: every compression incl. PIZ / PXR24 / B44(A) / DWAA / DWAB / HTJ2K / ZSTD, tiled level 0, multi-part first RGB(A)/Y/`layer.RGB` part; in-house NONE/RLE/ZIPS/ZIP reader is the fallback when the DLL is missing; unknown compression values or deep-only files probe `None` via `ExrFile.IsDecodable`; rebuild the DLL with `tools/openexr/build-openexr.sh`, never hand-write EXR codecs) are real HDR: `HdrKind.HdrRadiance` / `HdrKind.HdrExr`, linear scRGB (`HdrWicDecode.FromLinearFloatStill`), HDR badge, histogram/analysis and swapchain present. They decode at `PresentDecodeSize` like WIC: Radiance box-filters while streaming scanlines (a 16384x8192 pano never holds its 2 GB native float frame), EXR decodes native then `BoxScaleScrgb`; Info stats stay native. Their MaxCLL channel letter also comes from the decoder's stats pixels (`RadianceFrame` / `HdrFrame.MaxScrgbChannel`, also set by the WIC `Convert` and libavif `ToScrgb` paths via `GalleryPresent.PeakChannel` → `SetHdrStats` / `SetHdrPresentResult`); `GalleryPresent.MaxCllChannelFor` prefers it and only falls back to the box-filtered analysis channel when both peaks agree within 0.5%. EXR `chromaticities` are converted to BT.709 / D65 on decode; Info shows the source set as `<name> → scRGB` (`ExrFile.PrimariesName`: ACEScg, ACES2065-1, BT.2020, Display P3, DCI-P3, else "Custom primaries"; absent or BT.709 stays `BT.709 · scRGB`) via `HdrProbe.SourcePrimaries`. Gamut coverage (`CieGamut`) is a point-in-triangle test on xy with a 5e-4 edge tolerance; Rec.709 / P3 / Rec.2020 use their nominal D65 primaries, while AP1 / AP0 use the ACES primaries Bradford-adapted D60 → D65 (as decoded ACES EXRs land in scRGB), so a pure ACEScg primary reads as AP1, not AP0 / invalid. Gamut coverage is computed on presented scRGB (linear BT.709 primaries, negatives kept — BT.2020 PQ PNGs go through `GalleryPresent.PngEncodedToScrgb` / `Bt2020ToBt709` without clipping). The overlay / `GalleryWindow` Info card sits in a Grid row and scrolls (`ScrollViewer`) so it never runs under the bottom Details bar; PSD / HEIC / JXR / JXL / DDS are catalog stills without Magick. Catalog stills include `.avif` `.heic` `.heif` `.jxr` `.wdp` `.hdp` `.jxl` `.hdr` `.psd` `.dds` (`PathSafe.ImageExt`). Decode is inbox WIC (HEIF/AV1/JXL Store codecs) or C# RGBE, libavif for HDR AVIF only (`Starward.Codec` `avif.dll`); HDR JPEG XR (`.jxr` / `.wdp` / `.hdp`) presents via native WIC COM float/half into that same swapchain (WinRT has no float pixel format — do not `BitmapImage` the original). Not libjxl / Magick. HDR PNG and HDR HEIF present scRGB on Open via `SwapChainPanel` (`HdrSwapchainPresenter` / `GalleryStillSurface`) through WIC. HDR AVIF presents via libavif (`HdrAvifDecode` / `Starward.Codec` `avif.dll`: `avifDecoderNextImage` → `avifImageYUVToRGB` → PQ/HLG → scRGB), matching SKIV — identity matrix 0 is GBR. Honor primary-item `colr` via `pitm`/`ipma`. WIC remains fallback only; do not treat WIC `Rgba16` luma-in-R as RGB/GBR (red tint MaxCLL scRGB 207.561 or green Y→G). Ultra HDR JPEG stays the SDR base plus a label. `BitmapImage` remains the SDR fallback and the mosaic path — do **not** also `BitmapImage` the original when HDR present is attempted (that double-decodes 4K PQ). First HDR paint decodes at the **viewport** (`PresentDecodeSize`); luminance stats after present come from that downscaled/viewport frame (promote `HdrFrame` CIE Y / MaxCLL, or `TryMeasureAsync` via `MeasureDecodeSize` — viewport or `FastPresentLongEdge`, never a native 16384— decode). Math stays CIE Y in source primaries and MaxCLL scRGB. **HDR present never rasterizes on the UI thread**: `HdrSwapchainPresenter.TryPresentAsync` keeps COM / XAML work (layout, device, DXGI probe, `ResizeBuffers`, upload, `Present`) on the UI thread and runs `HdrRasterize.Fill` (float to half, parallel rows, reused `HdrHalfBuffer`) on the thread pool; it re-checks `_epoch` / frame / presenter (`stillCurrent`) after the raster and before any swapchain call, so a stale or closed-overlay result never presents. `GalleryStillSurface` requests presents through `HdrPresentCoalescer` (one loop; first paint and scale mode are immediate, resize / peak ticks settle 75 ms and are capped at 250 ms) - do not call the presenter directly or add a synchronous present. 1:1 re-decodes native. PNGs tagged only with an `iCCP` profile (no cICP, no `sRGB` chunk) are wide gamut when `IccProfile.MatchWideGamut` recognises Display P3 or BT.2020 colorants (D50-adapted or nominal, 0.004 xy) with an sRGB-like curve (`para` / single-gamma 2.1–2.5 or a `curv` table near sRGB at 0.5): they probe as `WideGamutPng` with primaries 12 / 9 and transfer 13 and convert like cICP P3 / 2020 (Info `Display P3 (ICC) · sRGB`); other ICC profiles stay plain sRGB. Files the scan flagged `Undecodable` show no Info / Details resolution unless the gallery decoded them (`FilePixelSize(..., undecodable)`; a `BitmapImage` of the original — not a thumb / large preview, `GalleryPresent.IsOriginalStill` — reports its size via `SetDecodedPixelSize`). PQ/HLG only when cICP transfer is 16/18 — cLLi/mDCv without transfer is sRGB, not PQ. **203 nits is BT.2408 paper / reference white**, not display peak — never label it “Display peak” and never clip auto present to 203 when DXGI is unknown (`EffectivePeakNits` / `ProbedDisplayLuminance` return 0; HDR rasterize then uses 10 000 nits). **SDR displays** (DXGI ColorSpace G22 sRGB, not advanced color / scRGB / HDR10) **tonemap** HDR stills: SKIV map-CLL-to-display + clip (`GalleryPresent.PresentMap` / `SdrPresentPeakNits` / `HdrColor.MapCllToDisplayScrgb`). G22 map target is always 80 nits (scRGB 1.0 composition white) — ignore EDID 80–220, dummy 270, and 203 paper white. G22 ColorSpace alone is not SDR: Windows HDR (SAM713F) often keeps G22 with dummy 270 — `IsHdrOutput` treats peak >220 as HDR clip-only scRGB (dummy 270 unknown peak → 10 000, not 203). DXGI probe failures (`TryQuery`, no adapter/output) must not throw past present or fall through to 80-nit SDR: `UnknownDisplayPresentsHdr` (PQ/HLG/HDR JXR) presents scRGB at unknown peak. Overlay Info `Display:` and `OutputDebugString` log CCD ACE / path count / DXGI cs+peak or the fail reason. SDR `PresentMap` uses sticky highest content MaxCLL (`StickyContentMaxNits` / `StickyContentMaxNitsForStill`), not the current `HdrFrame` decode size, so Fit viewport vs 1:1 native share one scale (header cLLi is a floor; Info MaxCLL stays the pixel peak). That map peak is then capped at 2x the frame's sampled P99 max-RGB (`GalleryPresent.SdrMapPeakNits` / `HdrFrame.P99MaxRgbNits`, floor 80 nits) so a tiny extreme highlight (the sun in a 130 000-nit `.hdr` panorama) does not scale the whole frame to black; typical HDR stills keep the MaxCLL map. The sticky peak is **per still** — next/prev must not keep a prior MaxCLL. HDR displays keep scRGB present + Settings Peak override (`GalleryPeak`). Info **Display luminance** is DXGI `MaxFullFrameLuminance` (else `MaxLuminance`) when it looks like a real HDR peak (>220). **Max luminance / avg / min** are CIE Y in the source primaries **before** 2020→709 (`LuminanceY`); **MaxCLL (scRGB)** is max channel after the matrix / 80 — not cLLi metadata nits. **Resolution** is file pixels (`FilePixelSize`: WIC/native, then header `ImageDimensions`, then catalog) — never a 512 thumb when the file is 3840×2160. App-wide **Peak** override lives on Settings (`TglHdrPeakOverride` / `SldHdrPeakNits` / `TxtHdrPeakNits`, Fluent + text, LocalSettings via `GalleryPeak`); present uses that global clip when override is on. Do not put Peak on overlay or gallery-window chrome. The former top-left Info flyout (`BrdGalleryImageInfo`) is removed — its fields live in `ViewerDetailsCard` (File / Color & HDR / Histogram / Gamut / Tags / Generation). **Histogram + HDR analysis** (`HdrAnalysis.Analyze` / `AnalyzePacked8`) is **one shared pass** over the presented `HdrFrame` (viewport decode, not the 512 thumb, not Magick / a second viewer) that yields the histogram bins, light stats, gamut coverage and the CIE 1931 xy density together — do not add a second per-feature pass. Skip online-only and API thumbs (`ShouldBuild`). Luma is CIE Y in the **source** primaries (`HdrAnalysis.PixelNits` = `LumaNitsFromPresentedScrgb`, same as Info) and the heatmap uses that same function, so the histogram's HDR section and heatmap colours always agree. The chart (`GalleryHistogramChart`) follows Sacb0y's Lightroom reference: grey luminance area under translucent R/G/B fills, x axis from `HistogramScale` — an **SDR section** (sRGB-encoded, 0 → 203-nit reference white, which is where the decoders put SDR white; a reference white, never a display peak) then an **HDR section** in whole stops (`StopCount` = ceil(log2(max / 203)) clamped 1–6; SDR stills have no HDR section) with dashed stop lines and an **accent** tint; then a gradient bar (SDR black→white, HDR accent; the heatmap palette when the heatmap is on), then **format · index in view (`5/33`) · file pixels (file size)** and **camera EXIF** (`MetadataExtractorService.ReadCamera`, local only) or, without camera EXIF, AI **Model · Sampler · Steps · Seed** (`GalleryDetails`). **No clipping warning** (no triangle, no toggle). Luma / RGB toggles are independent but never both off (`ToggleLayer`). GalleryWindow **Details** shows the full chart (`BtnGalleryWindowHistogramLuma` / `BtnGalleryWindowHistogramRgb`, `TxtGalleryWindowHistogram`, `TxtGalleryWindowHistogramFormat` / `Index` / `Size` / `Exif`) plus the gamut view (`GalleryGamutChart`: CIE 1931 xy plot with spectral locus, Rec.709 / P3 / Rec.2020 / AP1 triangles, D65 and pixel density, plus SKIV's coverage % for 709 / P3 / 2020 / AP1 / AP0 / invalid, `ImgGalleryWindowCie`, `TxtGalleryWindowGamut*`); the compact chart under Info (`TxtGalleryWindowInfoHistogram`) and the compact chart + gamut in overlay Info (`TxtGalleryOverlayHistogram`, `ImgGalleryOverlayCie`) stay in the top-left Info card so they do not cover `MediaPlayer` transport. UIA: assert those `Txt*` ids (Canvas has a weak peer). Details card Color & HDR section includes MaxCLL channel (`MaxCLL (scRGB): 12.5 (B)`), **P99** luminance, **FALL** labelled as Palace's own figure (`FALL (Palace, avg of max RGB)` — SKIV has no MaxFALL), % above SDR white and the gamut summary; hide HDR rows for SDR. **Heatmap** (`BtnGalleryHeatmap` / `BtnGalleryWindowHeatmap`, Ctrl+H, `ShowHeatmap`; enabled only while an HDR swapchain present exists, `CanShowHeatmap`) re-rasters the cached frame through `HdrPixelMap` (`HdrVizMode.Heatmap`) with SKIV's 9-stop D2D palette (`HdrHeatmap`, 0 / 3.16 / 10 / 31.6 / 100 / 316 / 1000 / 3160 / 10000 nits), palette white = 203 nits on HDR displays and scRGB 1.0 on SDR; it measures the source pixel before tonemap. `HdrPixelMap` / `HdrAnalysis` / `CieDiagram` are pure and are the shared code for the planned Save As / export / conversion work (its own PR) — reuse them there instead of copying the tonemap or analysis math. `CurrentProbe` is assigned **before** `CurrentPath` / `PreviewImageUri` / `IsImage`, then `StillRevision` is bumped once — `GalleryStillSurface` refreshes on `StillRevision`, not each field. `Bind` of the same gallery is a no-op; `Bind(null)` / Unloaded increment `_epoch` so an in-flight WIC decode cannot present onto a closed overlay. `ScpHdr` lives inside `ScrStill`; Actual/Fill size content from oriented `HdrFrame` or `BitmapImage` PixelWidth/Height after `ImageOpened`. Cache `HdrFrame` by path+probe — `SizeChanged` / `Scaling` re-present when a frame is cached (not only when `ScpHdr` is already Visible). Present uses layout DIPs (`Width` / `ScrStill`), never a Collapsed `ActualWidth` of 0; show `ScpHdr` under the SDR image, then hide the image on success. A still URI that is not `item.Path` (thumb / cloud preview) must `HideHdr` and clear the cache. WIC decode uses `OrientedPixelWidth` / `OrientedPixelHeight` with `RespectExifOrientation`. `ProbeDisplay` matches the window's monitor (`MonitorFromWindow`), not `EnumOutputs(0)`. CCD is `TryWindowsHdrEnabled(DeviceName)` only — do **not** `TryWindowsHdrEnabled(null)` after a named non-HDR (`WindowsHdrForNamedOutput` ignores any-path HDR). `CreateSwapChainForComposition` is vtable 24, `GetDesc1` is 27, and `SetColorSpace1` must be `DXGI_COLOR_SPACE_RGB_FULL_G10_NONE_P709` (1) or present fails. 8-bit unpack uses `HdrPixels` and the actual WIC format (Rgba8 is not BGRA).- Video posters use `StorageFile.GetThumbnailAsync` (shell/provider stream), not `BitmapDecoder` on the original. Overlay play uses `MediaPlayer.Play()` (`BtnGalleryPlay`). Overlay / GalleryWindow **Set thumb** (`BtnGallerySetThumb` / `BtnGalleryWindowSetThumb`) replaces the mosaic JPEG from the current seek position for playable local video only (`VideoMosaicThumb` / `VideoFrameThumb` → `MediaComposition.GetThumbnailAsync` + `ThumbnailService.CacheScaledJpegAsync`); never beside the source, never hydrate cloud originals just for a poster.
- Video volume chrome: `VolumeControl` / `GalleryVolume` (mute remembers prior level; unmute-from-0 → 50%; hover/focus expands slider pill; wheel ±5 / Shift ±1; M / Up / Down; HUD; LocalSettings `GalleryVolume` / `GalleryVolumeMuted`; stock volume button hidden). Do not cover `MediaPlayer` transport.
